From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:56:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 073/111] Scroll map weighs headings, tables and code by their
 drawn size

The preview position of a source line was counted in plain text lines,
so headings (up to twice the text size, with space above), table rows
(cell padding) and code blocks (smaller text, padded block) drifted the
map: in a long document the outline in Preview could highlight the
heading just scrolled out of view. Each line now counts the size the
Markdown widget draws it with (Settings::with_text_size): heading sizes
by level plus their top padding, table rows with their padding, code at
0.875 with the block padding on the fence lines, and the real spacing
between blocks. A setext underline is not drawn and counts nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

